{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{G} \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Mor_{\\textit{Ab}(X)}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Mor_{\\textit{Ab}(Y)}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$f$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\varphi_x : \\mathcal{G}_{f(x)} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}_x\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-f-map}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee6226d8d3cfa9f0799ec4e26a2b8057236456ac8f46541fea927d1b1da0f5c3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b86d9a456057a01e9cff92d664bad17f7cf7d18322c5274e749860875f3f96d2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nGiven a continuous map <MATH_0001> and sheaves of abelian\ngroups <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> on <MATH_0005>, the notion\nof an <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0006>-map <MATH_0007>\nof sheaves of abelian groups<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> makes sense. We can just define\nit exactly as in Definition <REF_0001> (replacing maps\nof sets with homomorphisms of abelian groups) or we can\nsimply say that it is the same as a map of abelian\nsheaves <MATH_0008>. We will use this\nnotion freely in the following. The group of <MATH_0009>-maps between\n<MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> will be in canonical bijection\nwith the groups\n<MATH_0012>\nand\n<MATH_0013>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nComposition of <MATH_0014>-maps is defined in exactly the\nsame manner as in the case of <MATH_0015>-maps of sheaves of\nsets. In addition, given an <MATH_0016>-map <MATH_0017>\nas above, the induced maps on stalks\n<MATH_0018>\nare abelian group homomorphisms.\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2a205c765773b0905f1d8c3300dcd4d34618159ae58064a7b34a7a3058e406bc", "unit_id": "tag:008N:prose-0002"}
